 ("H-M1", "hydro", "major", "The -30 %/+10 % band was far too narrow at 0.5-0.6 m/s: the 0.5 m/s point sits on the polar 'cliff' (NACA 4412 best L/D 10 at Re 4e4 vs 39 at 6e4); shifting the transition Reynolds number by 1.5 moves the 0.5 m/s output by -62 %/+46 %.",
  "Re/1.5 and Re x1.5 sensitivities added (polar lookup Reynolds number scaled); the band is now computed per flow from the full one-at-a-time envelope and quoted per flow.",
  f"band {b.get('0.5', {}).get('lo', 0)*100:+.0f}/{b.get('0.5', {}).get('hi', 0)*100:+.0f} % at 0.5, {b.get('0.7', {}).get('lo', 0)*100:+.0f}/{b.get('0.7', {}).get('hi', 0)*100:+.0f} % at 0.7, {b.get('1.0', {}).get('lo', 0)*100:+.0f}/{b.get('1.0', {}).get('hi', 0)*100:+.0f} % at 1.0 m/s; Re/1.5: {sens.get('Re / 1.5 (earlier transition)', [0]*10)[VS.index(0.5)]:.2f} / {sens.get('Re / 1.5 (earlier transition)', [0]*10)[VS.index(1.0)]:.2f} W at 0.5 / 1.0"),
 ("H-M2", "hydro", "major", "The 3-vs-2-blade margin (4 %) is inside the polar uncertainty and the selection flips under the corrected start gate (TSR 1.75 three-blade or five-blade designs win when self-start at 0.5-0.6 m/s is required).",
  "Both sweep stages re-run with the corrected start gate and a per-blade-count hub-packaging constraint; stage 2 broadened to 3/4/5 blades; the selection and the hand-started alternative are both reported; model/robustness_v4.py re-evaluates the best candidate per blade count under the baseline, Re/1.5, Re x1.5 and the upper-bound start model.",
  "see REPORT section 4 (robustness table) and selection.json"),
